text: ['All creatures with flying able to block Talruum Piper do so.', "As an additional cost to cast this spell, return X Swamps you control to their owner's hand.\\nInfernal Harvest deals X damage divided as you choose among any number of target creatures.", 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a creature.\\nTarget creature gets +4/+2 until end of turn.', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a green creature.\\nSearch your library for a green creature card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice all permanents you control and discard your hand.\\nTarget player loses 5 life.', 'At the beginning of each end step, each player who tapped a land for mana this turn sacrifices a land. Desolation deals 2 damage to each player who sacrificed a Plains this way.', "At the beginning of each player's draw step, that player puts the cards in their hand on the bottom of their library in any order, then draws that many cards.", "At the beginning of each player's upkeep, that player chooses artifact, creature, land, or non-Aura enchantment. All nontoken permanents of that type phase out. (While they're phased out, they're treated as though they don't exist. Each one phases in before its controller untaps during their next untap step.)", "At the beginning of each player's upkeep, that player exiles a card at random from their hand. The player may play that card this turn. At the beginning of the next end step, if the player hasn't played the card, they put it into their graveyard.", "At the beginning of each player's upkeep, that player may sacrifice a creature. If that player doesn't, they lose 5 life and you sacrifice Pillar Tombs of Aku.", "At the beginning of your upkeep, for each land target player controls in excess of the number you control, choose a land that player controls, then the chosen permanents phase out. Repeat this process for artifacts and creatures. (While they're phased out, they're treated as though they don't exist. They phase in before that player untaps during their next untap step.)", 'Attacking creatures with flying get -2/-2 and lose flying until end of turn.', "Choose a card name, then target opponent mills a card. If a card with the chosen name was milled this way, you draw a card.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Choose one —\\n• Destroy target artifact creature.\\n• Attacking creatures get +1/+0 until end of turn.\\n• Target creature with power 2 or less can't be blocked this turn.", 'Choose one —\\n• Target creature gains first strike until end of turn.\\n• Target player gains 2 life.\\n• Destroy target Aura.', "Choose one —\\n• Target player discards a card.\\n• Target creature gets +2/-1 until end of turn.\\n• Target creature gains swampwalk until end of turn. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)", "Choose one —\\n• Target player mills four cards.\\n• Choose a land type and a basic land type. Each land of the first chosen type becomes the second chosen type until end of turn.\\n• Target artifact phases out. (While it's phased out, it's treated as though it doesn't exist. It phases in before its controller untaps during their next untap step.)", 'Choose one —\\n• Untap target permanent.\\n• Destroy target non-Aura enchantment.\\n• Target creature loses flying until end of turn.', "Coral Atoll enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Coral Atoll enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you return an untapped Island you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {C}{U}.", "Counter target spell. If an artifact or creature spell is countered this way, put that card onto the battlefield under your control instead of into its owner's graveyard.", "Creatures don't untap during their controllers' untap steps.\\nAt the beginning of each player's upkeep, that player may choose any number of tapped nongreen creatures they control and pay {2} for each creature chosen this way. If the player does, untap those creatures.", 'Creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', "Cumulative upkeep {1} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, put a rust counter on each artifact target opponent controls. Then destroy each artifact with mana value less than or equal to the number of rust counters on it. Artifacts destroyed this way can't be regenerated.\\nWhen Corrosion leaves the battlefield, remove all rust counters from all permanents.", "Cumulative upkeep {1} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nBlack creatures can't attack you.\\nNonblack creatures can't attack you unless their controller pays {2} for each creature they control that's attacking you.", 'Cumulative upkeep {1} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nWhen you play a card, sacrifice Juju Bubble.\\n{2}: You gain 1 life.', "Cumulative upkeep {R} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nBlue creatures can't block creatures you control.\\nNonblue creatures can't block creatures you control unless their controller pays 1 life for each blocking creature they control.", "Destroy all creatures with power 4 or greater. They can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy target artifact, enchantment, or land.', "Dormant Volcano enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Dormant Volcano enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you return an untapped Mountain you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {C}{R}.", 'Each land is a Swamp in addition to its other land types.', 'Each player draws X cards.', "Each player skips their untap step.\\nAt the beginning of each player's upkeep, that player simultaneously untaps each tapped artifact, creature, and land they control and taps each untapped artifact, creature, and land they control.", 'Enchant creature an opponent controls\\nWhenever enchanted creature becomes tapped, you draw a card.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1.\\nSacrifice a creature: Regenerate enchanted creature.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+3.\\n{W}: Return enchanted creature to its owner's hand.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has trample.\\nWhenever all non-Wall creatures you control attack, enchanted creature gets +X/+0 until end of turn, where X is the number of attacking creatures.', "Enchant creature\\nWhen Vampirism enters the battlefield, draw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1 for each other creature you control.\\nOther creatures you control get -1/-1.", 'Enchant creature\\nWhen enchanted creature dies, its controller loses life equal to its power and you gain life equal to its toughness.', 'Enchant creature\\nWhen enchanted creature is dealt damage, destroy it.', "Enchant creature\\n{U}{U}: Enchanted creature phases out. (While it's phased out, it's treated as though it doesn't exist. It phases in before its controller untaps during their next untap step.)", "Everglades enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Everglades enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you return an untapped Swamp you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {C}{B}.", "Exile the top three cards of your library face down. You may look at those cards for as long as they remain exiled. Until your next turn, you may play those cards. At the beginning of your next upkeep, put any of those cards you didn't play into your graveyard.", "Fear (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)\\nWhenever Suq'Ata Assassin attacks and isn't blocked, defending player gets a poison counter. (A player with ten or more poison counters loses the game.)", 'First strike; reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)', 'First strike\\nSacrifice Brass-Talon Chimera: Put a +2/+2 counter on target Chimera creature. It gains first strike. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)', "First strike\\nWhen Nekrataal enters the battlefield, destroy target nonartifact, nonblack creature. That creature can't be regenerated.", 'First strike\\nWhenever Talruum Champion blocks or becomes blocked by a creature, that creature loses first strike until end of turn.', "Flanking (Whenever a creature without flanking blocks this creature, the blocking creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.)\\nFallen Askari can't block.", "Flanking (Whenever a creature without flanking blocks this creature, the blocking creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.)\\nWhen Knight of the Mists enters the battlefield, you may pay {U}. If you don't, destroy target Knight and it can't be regenerated.", 'Flanking (Whenever a creature without flanking blocks this creature, the blocking creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.)\\n{1}{W}: Each creature without flanking blocking Knight of Valor gets -1/-1 until end of turn. Activate only once each turn.', 'Flanking (Whenever a creature without flanking blocks this creature, the blocking creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.)\\n{1}{W}: The next 1 damage that would be dealt to Zhalfirin Crusader this turn is dealt to any target instead.', "Flanking (Whenever a creature without flanking blocks this creature, the blocking creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.)\\n{U}{U}: Teferi's Honor Guard phases out. (While it's phased out, it's treated as though it doesn't exist. It phases in before you untap during your next untap step.)", 'Flash', 'Flying, protection from red', 'Flying, trample\\nCumulative upkeep {U}{R} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)', 'Flying, vigilance', "Flying\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Waterspout Djinn unless you return an untapped Island you control to its owner's hand.", 'Flying\\nCloud Elemental can block only creatures with flying.', "Flying\\nPhasing (This phases in or out before you untap during each of your untap steps. While it's phased out, it's treated as though it doesn't exist.)", "Flying\\nPhasing (This phases in or out before you untap during each of your untap steps. While it's phased out, it's treated as though it doesn't exist.)\\nWhenever Shimmering Efreet phases in, target creature phases out. (It phases in before its controller untaps during their next untap step.)", 'Flying\\nSacrifice Daraja Griffin: Destroy target black creature.', 'Flying\\nSacrifice Tin-Wing Chimera: Put a +2/+2 counter on target Chimera creature. It gains flying. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)', 'Flying\\nWhen Bogardan Phoenix dies, exile it if it had a death counter on it. Otherwise, return it to the battlefield under your control and put a death counter on it.', "Flying\\nWhen Shrieking Drake enters the battlefield, return a creature you control to its owner's hand.", 'Flying\\n{1}{B}, Sacrifice a creature: Regenerate Wake of Vultures.', 'Flying\\n{G}: Kyscu Drake gets +0/+1 until end of turn. Activate only once each turn.\\nSacrifice Kyscu Drake and a creature named Spitting Drake: Search your library for a card named Viashivan Dragon, put that card onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'Flying\\n{R}: Spitting Drake gets +1/+0 until end of turn. Activate only once each turn.', 'Flying\\n{R}: Viashivan Dragon gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\n{G}: Viashivan Dragon gets +0/+1 until end of turn.', "Flying\\n{T}: If the top card of target player's graveyard is a creature card, put that card on top of that player's library.", "Flying\\n{U}{U}: Rainbow Efreet phases out. (While it's phased out, it's treated as though it doesn't exist. It phases in before you untap during your next untap step.)", "Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)\\nAt the beginning of the end step, return Viashino Sandstalker to its owner's hand. (Return it only if it's on the battlefield.)", 'Haste\\nFlanking (Whenever a creature without flanking blocks this creature, the blocking creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.)', "Hulking Cyclops can't block.", "If a player would draw a card, instead they draw a card and reveal it. If it's a creature card, that player discards it unless they pay 3 life.", 'If damage would be dealt to Lichenthrope, put that many -1/-1 counters on it instead.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, remove a -1/-1 counter from Lichenthrope.', "Islandwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)\\n{G}: Regenerate River Boa.", "Jungle Basin enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Jungle Basin enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you return an untapped Forest you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {C}{G}.", "Karoo enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Karoo enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you return an untapped Plains you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {C}{W}.", 'Look at the top four cards of your library. Put one of them into your hand and the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.', 'Mill four cards. Whenever a creature attacks this turn, it gets +1/+0 until end of turn for each creature card put into your graveyard this way.', "Ogre Enforcer can't be destroyed by lethal damage unless lethal damage dealt by a single source is marked on it.", "Phasing (This phases in or out before you untap during each of your untap steps. While it's phased out, it's treated as though it doesn't exist.)\\nCreatures with flying can't attack or block, and their activated abilities with {T} in their costs can't be activated.", "Phyrexian Marauder enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.\\nPhyrexian Marauder can't block.\\nPhyrexian Marauder can't attack unless you pay {1} for each +1/+1 counter on it.", 'Players can cast spells and activate abilities only during their own turns.', "Players have no maximum hand size.\\nAt the beginning of each player's draw step, that player draws an additional card, then discards a card.", 'Prevent the next 5 damage that would be dealt this turn to any number of targets, divided as you choose.', 'Protection from black', "Return Gossamer Chains to its owner's hand: Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt by target unblocked creature this turn.", "Return a Forest you control to its owner's hand: Untap target creature. Activate only once each turn.", 'Return target card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield. Put a +1/+1 counter on it.', "Return two target creatures to their owners' hands.", 'Reveal the first card you draw each turn. Whenever you reveal a basic land card this way, draw a card.', 'Rock Slide deals X damage divided as you choose among any number of target attacking or blocking creatures without flying.', 'Sacrifice Resistance Fighter: Prevent all combat damage target creature would deal this turn.', 'Sacrifice a land: Add one mana of any type the sacrificed land could produce.', 'Sacrifice a nontoken permanent. If you do, target opponent loses 2 life unless that player sacrifices a permanent or discards a card. You may repeat this process any number of times.', 'Search your library for a Plains card. If target opponent controls more lands than you, you may search your library for an additional Plains card. Reveal those cards, put them into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for a card, then shuffle and put that card on top. You lose 2 life.', 'Simoon deals 1 damage to each creature target opponent controls.', 'Simultaneously, all phased-out creatures phase in and all creatures with phasing phase out.', 'Spells cost {1} less to cast.', "Swampwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)", "Target creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", 'Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose a card from it. That player discards that card.', "Target player can't play lands this turn.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", 'Target player draws two cards.', "The next time a source of your choice would deal damage to any target this turn, prevent that damage. If damage from a red source is prevented this way, Honorable Passage deals that much damage to the source's controller.", "This turn and next turn, creatures can't attack, and players and permanents can't be the targets of spells or activated abilities.", "Trample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, return a green creature you control to its owner's hand.", "Trample\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if you don't control a creature named Keeper of Kookus, Kookus deals 3 damage to you and attacks this turn if able.\\n{R}: Kookus gets +1/+0 until end of turn.", 'Trample\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, put a +1/+1 counter on each creature each opponent controls.', 'Trample\\nSacrifice Lead-Belly Chimera: Put a +2/+2 counter on target Chimera creature. It gains trample. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)', 'Tremor deals 1 damage to each creature without flying.', 'Untap all creatures that attacked this turn. After this main phase, there is an additional combat phase followed by an additional main phase.', 'Vigilance\\nSacrifice Iron-Heart Chimera: Put a +2/+2 counter on target Chimera creature. It gains vigilance. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)', 'When Brood of Cockroaches is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, at the beginning of the next end step, you lose 1 life and return Brood of Cockroaches to your hand.', "When Bull Elephant enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you return two Forests you control to their owner's hand.", "When Eye of Singularity enters the battlefield, destroy each permanent with the same name as another permanent, except for basic lands. They can't be regenerated.\\nWhenever a permanent other than a basic land enters the battlefield, destroy all other permanents with that name. They can't be regenerated.", 'When Goblin Recruiter enters the battlefield, search your library for any number of Goblin cards, reveal them, then shuffle and put those cards on top in any order.', "When Man-o'-War enters the battlefield, return target creature to its owner's hand.", "When Ovinomancer enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you return three basic lands you control to their owner's hand.\\n{T}, Return Ovinomancer to its owner's hand: Destroy target creature. It can't be regenerated. That creature's controller creates a 0/1 green Sheep creature token.", "When Suleiman's Legacy enters the battlefield, destroy all Djinns and Efreets. They can't be regenerated.\\nWhenever a Djinn or Efreet enters the battlefield, destroy it. It can't be regenerated.", 'When Tar Pit Warrior becomes the target of a spell or ability, sacrifice it.', 'When Uktabi Orangutan enters the battlefield, destroy target artifact.', "Whenever Dwarven Vigilantes attacks and isn't blocked, you may have it deal damage equal to its power to target creature. If you do, Dwarven Vigilantes assigns no combat damage this turn.", 'Whenever Goblin Swine-Rider becomes blocked, it deals 2 damage to each attacking creature and each blocking creature.', "Whenever Pygmy Hippo attacks and isn't blocked, you may have defending player activate a mana ability of each land they control and lose all unspent mana. If you do, Pygmy Hippo assigns no combat damage this turn and at the beginning of your next main phase this turn, you add an amount of {C} equal to the amount of mana that player lost this way.", 'Whenever Raging Gorilla blocks or becomes blocked, it gets +2/-2 until end of turn.', 'Whenever a player casts a red spell, you may pay {R}. If you do, Lightning Cloud deals 1 damage to any target.', 'Whenever an enchantment is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, draw a card.', 'White creatures you control have protection from black.\\nBlack creatures you control have protection from white.', "You may cast Mystic Veil as though it had flash. If you cast it any time a sorcery couldn't have been cast, the controller of the permanent it becomes sacrifices it at the beginning of the next cleanup step.\\nEnchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has shroud. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", 'You may cast Necromancy as though it had flash. If you cast it any time a sorcery couldn\'t have been cast, the controller of the permanent it becomes sacrifices it at the beginning of the next cleanup step.\\nWhen Necromancy enters the battlefield, if it\'s on the battlefield, it becomes an Aura with "enchant creature put onto the battlefield with Necromancy." Put target creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under your control and attach Necromancy to it. When Necromancy leaves the battlefield, that creature\'s controller sacrifices it.', "You may cast Parapet as though it had flash. If you cast it any time a sorcery couldn't have been cast, the controller of the permanent it becomes sacrifices it at the beginning of the next cleanup step.\\nCreatures you control get +0/+1.", "You may cast Relic Ward as though it had flash. If you cast it any time a sorcery couldn't have been cast, the controller of the permanent it becomes sacrifices it at the beginning of the next cleanup step.\\nEnchant artifact\\nEnchanted artifact has shroud. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", "You may cast Spider Climb as though it had flash. If you cast it any time a sorcery couldn't have been cast, the controller of the permanent it becomes sacrifices it at the beginning of the next cleanup step.\\nEnchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +0/+3 and has reach. (It can block creatures with flying.)", 'You may play up to three additional lands this turn.', "You may sacrifice two Mountains rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nFireblast deals 4 damage to any target.", '{0}: Chronatog gets +3/+3 until end of turn. You skip your next turn. Activate only once each turn.', '{1}: Regenerate Matopi Golem. When it regenerates this way, put a -1/-1 counter on it.', '{2}, Sacrifice Triangle of War: Target creature you control fights target creature an opponent controls. (Each deals damage equal to its power to the other.)', '{3}, {T}: Create a 0/1 colorless Prism artifact creature token.\\nSacrifice a Prism token: Add one mana of any color.', "{3}, {T}: Target creature you control gets +2/+2 until end of turn. Return it to its owner's hand at the beginning of the next end step. (Return it only if it's on the battlefield.)", '{3}{B}{B}, Sacrifice a creature: Return Necrosavant from your graveyard to the battlefield. Activate only during your upkeep.', '{4}: Put a pressure counter on Magma Mine.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Magma Mine: It deals damage equal to the number of pressure counters on it to any target.', '{B}, Sacrifice Urborg Mindsucker: Target opponent discards a card at random. Activate only as a sorcery.', '{G}, Sacrifice Giant Caterpillar: Create a 1/1 green Insect creature token with flying named Butterfly at the beginning of the next end step.', "{G}, {T}: Target land becomes a 2/2 green creature that's still a land. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)", '{R}: Keeper of Kookus gains protection from red until end of turn.', '{T}, Sacrifice a land: Destroy target land.', "{T}: Add one mana of any color. During your next untap step, as you untap your permanents, return Undiscovered Paradise to its owner's hand.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Quicksand: Target attacking creature without flying gets -1/-2 until end of turn.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Untap target Griffin. If it's a creature, it gets +1/+1 until end of turn.", '{T}: Add {C}{C}.', '{T}: Counter target spell unless its controller pays {1} and 1 life.', "{T}: Look at the top card of target player's library. If it's a nonland card, you may pay 2 life. If you do, put it into that player's graveyard.", '{T}: Target attacking creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', "{U}{U}, Return two Islands you control to their owner's hand: Return target creature to its owner's hand.", '{W}, Pay 2 life: The next time a source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', "{W}, {T}: Target creature can't block this turn.", '{X}, Sacrifice Snake Basket: Create X 1/1 green Snake creature tokens. Activate only as a sorcery.', '{X}: Crypt Rats deals X damage to each creature and each player. Spend only black mana on X.']
flavor: ['"\'I\'ve seen hornworms big as a man\'s fist,\' the traveler said, and nodded soberly when our jaws went slack at his ignorance."\\n—Afari, *Tales*', '"A beauty made more so by its fleeting visitations."\\n—Teferi', '"A burst of hot air tossed the moon into the air, and the moon liked it up there so much it never needed the ground again."\\n—Azeworai, "Glitter Moon"', '"A pretty toy. Now show me its tactical applications."\\n—Telim\'Tor', '"Ah, I remember my first death."\\n—Zarkuu, necrosavant', '"Aku, City of Hidden Graves / Aku, City of Lost Kings / Aku, welcome me."\\n—Pillar tomb inscription', '"And darkness shall be cast from me\\nFor my soul resides in the Sun."\\n—Femeref dirge', '"And the flamingos said, \'Get out of our nest—we can\'t be seen with the likes of you!\' So, the griffin ate them."\\n—Azeworai, "The Ugly Bird"', '"As the winds abated, there was a shower of dragonscales, then nothing more."\\n—Azeworai, "The Unruly Wind"', '"As you breathe your last, understand why I accept such forbidden gifts."\\n—Purraj of Urborg', '"Ate up all of his siblings in the first week. A good beginning for one destined to command."\\n—Suka, ogre matron', '"Beauty to the eye does not always translate to the touch."\\n—Naimah, Femeref philosopher', '"But no one heard the snake\'s gentle hiss for peace over the elephant\'s trumpeting of war."\\n—Afari, *Tales*', '"But once, with a magician\'s help, Time was stopped and Day stood still."\\n—"Love Song of Night and Day"', '"By the tongues of a thousand serpents, this time I do not lie."\\n—Ahmahz il Kin, Suq\'Ata diplomat', '"Careless, like a child with fire, so was I with time."\\n—Teferi', '"Controlling time ensures you need never look impulsive again."\\n—Teferi', '"Do not underestimate the power of many against one."\\n—Sidar Jabari', '"Every temper tantrum makes another angry gorilla."\\n—Femeref children\'s myth', '"Far too many soldiers have died in their beds."\\n—Telim\'Tor', '"Fire is dead. Water has killed him."\\n—From *The Stories of Nature*', '"Flog and Squee / Up the tree / See the army / Flee, flee, flee."\\n—Goblin nursery rhyme/war cry', '"Fly us higher, out of its storm."\\n—Sisay, Captain of the *Weatherlight*', '"Good is not a \'thing.\' You can neither touch nor own it. No, Good is a vision we all share and strive to make real."\\n—Asmira, Holy Avenger', '"Good ol\' rock. Nothing beats rock."\\n—Rhirhok, goblin archer', '"Harah swung his sword mightily, but still the air held him fast."\\n—Azeworai, "Kenechi\'s Dream"', '"He blows a gust across the cliff to vanish in a breath of wind."\\n—"Song of the Wind Being"', '"He traded sand for skins, skins for gold, gold for life. In the end, he traded life for sand."\\n—Afari, *Tales*', '"How can you claim the gods are merciless when they robbed the snake of its limbs to give the other creatures a sporting chance?"\\n—Hakim, Loreweaver', '"How have I angered nature that she would imprison me in a labyrinth of grass?"\\n—Kasib ibn Naji, Letters', '"I have heard terrible tales of black rains, ashen fields, and metal that screams. I have consoled myself that the tales were a myth of some fevered mind. But today I saw a walker—and now I fear the truth."\\n—Kasib Ibn Naji, Letters', '"I have seen the horrors Kaervek has freed. My betrayal is certain—but of Kaervek or of Jamuraa, I cannot say."\\n—Jolrael', '"I offered you eternal life; I just didn\'t say *where*."\\n—Shauku, Endbringer', '"I write upon clean white parchment with a sharp quill and the blood of my students, divining their secrets."\\n—Shauku, Endbringer', '"I\'ve dreamt of a second harvest but fear I will not see it."\\n—Asmira, Holy Avenger', '"If a rhino\'s head is lower than its shoulders, trust me—it is *not* praying."\\n—Mwani, Mtenda herder', '"If it bears wings, I will pin it to the skies over Tefemburu."\\n—Ruya, Zhalfirin archer', '"If it can scar the sky with fire, do not share its destination."\\n—Mwani, Mtenda herder', '"If my heart had a lid, I would lift it and show you my joy."\\n—From Suq\'Ata wedding ceremony', '"Is it true that the apes wear furs of gold when they marry?"\\n—Rana, Suq\'Ata market fool', '"It\'s like waking on a bed of a thousand olives during an earthquake of subtle force."\\n—Afari, *Tales*', '"Its speed will be equaled only by the swiftness of my enemy\'s fall."\\n—Kaervek', '"Kaervek believes the drakes\' cries herald his victory; in truth, they mourn aloud for his impending demise."\\n—Teferi', '"Kaervek imprisoned Mangara out of jealousy, but he taints Jamuraa simply out of spite."\\n—Asmira, Holy Avenger', '"Kill a creature, destroy the present. Kill the land, destroy the future."\\n—Kaervek', '"Madness and genius are separated only by degrees of success."\\n—Sidar Jabari', '"Magic is my thread, my will the needle. I weave over you as if you never were."\\n—Poetics of Hanan', '"May you get the mount you deserve."\\n—Suq\'Ata curse', '"Mold could catch you."\\n—Suq\'Ata insult', '"My horizon was the arcing petals, my new home resplendent with spires of weeds and pillows of fragrant pollen."\\n—Naimah, Femeref philosopher', '"My mother once told me angels sing their swords\' names with each strike."\\n—Sisay, Captain of the *Weatherlight*', '"My pet will pick the ripe fruit from your tortured brain as if it were hanging from a vine."\\n—Kaervek', '"My soldiers fought without hesitation, died without doubt."\\n—Sidar Jabari', '"Never stop \'til you see your lance come out the other side."\\n—Telim\'Tor', '"Next!"', '"Oft have I wished to undo past deeds, but never did I imagine they would be undone for me."\\n—Naimah, Femeref philosopher', '"Once I dreamt of death, but now it dreams of me / And only rats and rotting flesh can hear my silent plea."\\n—Mundungu chant', '"Our buried kings silently await the revolt of dead peasants."\\n—Tuwile, mundungu of Aku', '"Our love is like the river in the summer season of long rains. / For a little while it spilled its banks, flooding the crops in the fields."\\n—"Love Song of Night and Day"', '"Respect the earth, for it will one day be your shield and another day your blanket."\\n—Liefellen, Quirion exarch', '"Retainer of eternal Sun! Life flash again upon thy wings."\\n—"Song to the Sun," Femeref song', '"So the vulture said to the griffin, \'You gonna eat that?\'"\\n—Azeworai, "The Ugly Bird"', '"Some believe Sandstalkers to be illusions; those with scars know better."\\n—*Zhalfirin Guide to the Desert*', '"Some say a great cyclops turns the world in its hands, looking down upon it with its one bright eye."\\n—Afari, *Tales*', '"Some say the sea is jealous of the land and wishes to climb its heights to meet the sky."\\n—Afari, *Tales*', '"Sometimes a burden can be borne only on the shoulders of a willing enemy."\\n—Suq\'Ata aphorism', '"That does it! I\'m going back to hunting chickens!"\\n—Rhirhok, goblin archer', '"The black-and-white sacred monkey holds her children to her, and waits."\\n—"Love Song of Night and Day"', '"The blood on my hands is merely proof of my ambition."\\n—Kaervek', '"The cyclops shrugged off savage blows, but casual insults made him weep."\\n—Azeworai, "The Cyclops who Couldn\'t"', '"The elves can hide better than most can look."\\n—Mwani, Mtenda herder', '"The end justifies the means. What do I care if I rule over the dead rather than over the living? The dead ask fewer questions."\\n—Kaervek', '"The land has been gracious enough to let you tread upon her for years. That privilege is about to end."\\n—Liefellen, Quirion exarch', '"The true dishonor for a soldier is surviving the war."\\n—Telim\'Tor', '"Their tears spill over Jamuraa. Mixed with blood, they wash everything red."\\n—"Love Song of Night and Day"', '"Then she spread a fine dust over the land, like a butterfly shaking its wing."\\n—"The Enchantress," Femeref tale', '"These things will protect you while I\'m gone, remind you of my love for you."\\n—"Love Song of Night and Day"', '"They may seem ceremonial, but their swords are still sharp."\\n—Kipkemboi, Kukemssa pirate', '"This is a war without neutrality."\\n—Asmira, Holy Avenger', '"This little prize will cover your head, your spells, your bets, and your behind!"\\n—Pashad ibn Asim, Suq\'Ata trader', '"Time may heal all wounds, but what heals time?"\\n—Teferi', '"Too much work—it takes a long time to break them in, and more than a few recruits."\\n—Grebog, goblin swine-rider', '"Tread upon the meek, and they shall wound your feet and make you crawl."\\n—Asmira, Holy Avenger', '"Uh, does anyone have a flute?"\\n—Rana, Suq\'Ata market fool', '"War is the crucible of leadership."\\n—Rashida Scalebane', '"Watch death wait / Wait, death, watch / Steal breath swiftly / but steal life slowly."\\n—Suq\'Ata dirge', '"We are to be bound together as the reeds of a basket."\\n—Asmira, Rashida, and Jabari, unity chant', '"Wealth is a good thing, compared to poverty—your food is better, your robes are softer, and your companions have bathed more recently."\\n—Kipkemboi, Kukemssa pirate', '"When you run you\'re graceful and swift, sleek as a powerful panther."\\n—"Love Song of Night and Day"', '"Where are falling feathers deadlier than falling rock?"\\n—*The One Thousand Questions*', '"Where do you run when the earth becomes your enemy?"\\n—Naimah, Femeref philosopher', '"Why is loud stupidity so infectious?"\\n—Rana, Suq\'Ata market fool', '"With Rashida\'s blades, my guiding vision and the luck of the blessed, today we will free Mangara!"\\n—Asmira, Holy Avenger', '"With no further options, I was forced to don the mask."\\n—Rashida Scalebane', '"With this ring, you have friends in worlds you\'ve never heard of."\\n—Sisay, Captain of the *Weatherlight*', '"You know you\'ve angered the gods when the clouds turn against you."\\n—Sisay, Captain of the *Weatherlight*', '"You stop breathing for just a few minutes and everyone jumps to conclusions."\\n—Zarkuu, necrosavant', '"Your arrogance amazes me, Kaervek. Did you not know the price you would pay?"\\n—Mangara', ". . . but the price of Mangara's freedom was Asmira's life.", 'A rhino\'s bargain\\n—Femeref expression meaning "a situation with no choices"', "Asmira's prayers alone should have freed Mangara from the amber prison . . .", 'BOOM!', "Embermages aren't well known for their diplomatic skills.", 'Fear the mists, for they are armed.', 'First the insult, then the injury.', 'For the chronatog, there is no meal like the present.', 'Four gray trees and a long, coiling snake. What am I?\\n—Zhalfirin riddle', "If you find yourself and a friend being chased by a King Cheetah, you have but one chance: Trip your friend.\\n—Suq'Ata wisdom", 'In the Talruum language, there is no word for "surprised."', 'In troubled times, there are few greater sorrows than a wayward savior.', 'It prefers its meals cooked.', "Jolrael's choice of homes was far better than her choice of allies.", 'Life or death: which is the illusion?"\\n—Naimah, Femeref philosopher', 'Prayers for rain are answered with the thunder of hooves.', 'Purraj sang slaughter and danced death.', 'Some dwarves can only be pushed so far.', 'Some potmakers claim to use the mud of such creatures to make their finest bowls—and that the bowls scream when fired.', 'The Viashivan understand that cruelty arises from opportunity.', 'The Zhalfirin war triangle represents a trinity of might, faith, and guile.', 'The lion blinked\\n—Femeref expression meaning "situation avoided"', 'The mightiest clouds sit upon spires of fire.\\n—Femeref adage', "There is no wall that can't be improved by making it taller.", "Wanted: Thick-skinned goblin for guarding mean ol' Kookus. Must like fires. Must heal quickly.", 'When the Talruum began to play, the dragons fell from the sky to squash the obnoxious noise.', 'Wind will win, whatever we wish.', "With Suleiman's ascension to power, the djinn and efreets of ancient Rabiah learned humility.", "You'll never miss what you never had."]
artist: ['Adam Rex', 'Adrian Smith', 'Alan Rabinowitz', 'Andrew Robinson', 'Blackie del Rio', 'Bob Eggleton', 'Brian Horton', 'Bryan Talbot', 'Cecil Fernando', 'Christopher Rush', 'Cliff Nielsen', 'Craig Hooper', 'D. Alexander Gregory', 'Dan Frazier', "David O'Connor", 'David Seeley', 'DiTerlizzi', 'Donato Giancola', 'Douglas Shuler', 'Eric Peterson', 'Gary Gianni', 'Gary Leach', 'Geofrey Darrow & I. Rabarot', 'George Pratt', 'Gerry Grace', 'Greg Spalenka', 'Harold McNeill', 'Ian Miller', 'Jeff Miracola', 'Jerry Tiritilli', 'John Avon', 'John Coulthart', 'John Matson', 'Jon J Muth', 'Kaja Foglio', 'Kev Walker', 'Mark Poole', 'Michael Danza', 'Mike Dringenberg', 'Mike Kerr', 'Nathalie Hertz', 'Nicola Leonard', 'Omaha Pérez', 'Paul Lee', 'Pete Venters', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Richard Kane Ferguson', 'Roger Raupp', 'Romas Kukalis', 'Ron Spencer', 'Scott Hampton', 'Scott Kirschner', 'Steve Luke', 'Steve White', 'Stuart Griffin', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Thomas Gianni', 'Tom Kyffin', 'Tony Roberts', 'Una Fricker', 'Zina Saunders']
